          "caption": "Yağlıkçı Hacı Reşit Bey Yalısı and Prenses Rukiye Yalısı, the Yalı mansions on the Bosphorus shore in Istanbul, Turkey. Located at Kanlıca, they were built in the 1850s. The manor Prenses Rukiye Yalisi was given as a gift to Rukiye princess, the daughter of the governor of Ottoman Egypt, Abbas Halim Pasa. The house is surrounded by planting Mihrabad.",
